### Did the Abortion Legislation Act 2020 remove or relax any previous New Zealand legal restrictions on abortion methods that were considered controversial before 2020?
Answer: Yes, the Abortion Legislation Act 2020 removed previous legal restrictions on controversial abortion methods, as the source states that under the new law, "There will be no legal restrictions on controversial methods of abortion such as intact dilation and extraction abortions (also knows as partial-birth abortions)." This indicates that prior to 2020, such methods were legally restricted in New Zealand.

